# Line endings: LF in the repository *and* in the working tree, on every machine.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows gives the working tree CRLF while macOS gets
# LF, so the same file has two byte representations depending on which machine
# it was checked out on. Two things in this repo care:
#
#   - `.claude/hooks/*.sh` and `*.py` are executed directly. A CRLF shebang is
#     a syntax error to a POSIX interpreter, so a Windows checkout produces
#     hooks that cannot run.
#   - Generated artifacts inherit the line endings of the template they were
#     read from (templateRenderer joins on \n, but hands back an unrendered
#     body verbatim), so artifacts differ by authoring machine.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content on its own; the media files
# are pinned anyway so no heuristic has to be right about them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.vsix binary
